## 3. Extracting Hidden API Endpoints
Many modern Single Page Applications (SPAs built with React, Vue, or Angular) load API routes dynamically. You can use Puppeteer to listen to background network chatter to hunt for hidden IDORs or open endpoints. [1] 

// Listen to all network requests made by the page
page.on('request', request => {
  const url = request.url();
  if (url.includes('/api/v')) {
    console.log(`[API Found]: ${url} [Method]: ${request.method()}`);
  }
});
await page.goto('https://target.com');

## 4. DOM-based Race Conditions
You can open 10 or 20 headless browser pages simultaneously inside a single script execution block to hammer an API endpoint or submit forms at the exact same millisecond to test for business logic flaws and race conditions.
## 5. Automated Screenshotting for Subdomain Takeovers
When scanning thousands of subdomains, use Puppeteer to capture visual screenshots of every alive domain. You can quickly scroll through the images to look for signature cloud hosting error screens (e.g., "AWS 404", "GitHub Pages NoSuchBucket") signaling an easy takeover.

await page.goto('https://target.com');await page.screenshot({ path: 'subdomain_evidence.png' });

