Many modern desktop apps (like Discord, Slack, or trading terminals) run on Electron (JavaScript) or C++. This script uses Puppeteer to grab API keys, then uses Frida to intercept system memory or file writes of the desktop application to dynamically read/write backend flags.

import puppeteer from 'puppeteer';import frida from 'frida';
async function runDesktopBounty() {
